<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · river</p><h1 class="enc-title">Olt River</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Olt is a river of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/romania">Romania</a>, about 615 km long, that rises in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/eastern-carpathians">Eastern Carpathians</a>, flows through south-eastern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/transylvania">Transylvania</a>, cuts through the Southern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/carpathian-mountains">Carpathians</a> by the Red Tower Pass and runs south to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/danube">Danube</a>. It divides Wallachia into <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/oltenia">Oltenia</a>, named after it, to the west and Muntenia to the east.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/olt-river.jpg" alt="Olt River" width="320" height="197" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Stefan Bichler · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Olt_East_Karpatien.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
